WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.220
A dark hovel against a cottage wall.

2
00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:06.490
Through a chink: an old man with a guitar,

3
00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:08.370
a man reading aloud.

4
00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:12.470
A huge shadowed hand
traces letters in the dust.

5
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:16.890
One day he will tell his maker:
"I was benevolent and good;

6
00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:19.320
misery made me a fiend."

7
00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:22.310
Then a stage in 1823.

8
00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:25.000
A cloaked figure stands in the footlights.

9
00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:27.280
His speech bubble stays empty.

10
00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:30.580
In the novel, the monster
speaks better than his maker.

11
00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:33.010
So why give him the best lines?

12
00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:35.570
In this mission, you'll
follow his education,

13
00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:37.850
from the senses to rejection.

14
00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:40.870
And you'll see how stage
and screen took his voice,

15
00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:43.640
right up to a 1931 film.

16
00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:47.740
Your mission: work out why
Shelley gives him the best lines.
